      "message": "fix(machine): remove unverified -360..360 A limit on microARC 4\n\nTormach mill operator manuals (UM10587 / UM10864 / UM10349, Rotational\nAxis) specify that PathPilot treats the A axis as a wrapped linear axis\nincreasing/decreasing without limit toward +/- infinity, and TD10749\ndescribes continuous harmonic-drive rotation with no travel limits or\nlimit switches. PathPilot Hub readings (v2.14.4, 770MX SIM) also reached\nA 1484.663 continuously and ran G1 A370 / G93 A400 without alarm.\n\nRemove the invented -360..360 A travel object from\nassets/machines/tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch (unstated = no limit under\nCamCraft's unstated-limit law) and cite the public Tormach manuals and\nHub readings in general.description. Update machine docs, guide page,\nand tests to pin continuous multi-turn wrapped A and Rotary Offset past\n1484.663 degrees while keeping bounded-travel refusal pins intact.\n\nFixes #2471\n\nCo-Authored-By: Antigravity (Gemini) <noreply@google.com>",
